2. INCLUDED 3D HOUGH TRANSFORM SOURCE
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The source code used for the 3D Hough-transform line reconstruction is
included under:

    3d_hough_transform/

This directory contains the Hough-transform source, Makefile, and BSD
license.

The analysis workflows below begin from previously generated Hough-line
outputs, so recompiling and rerunning the Hough transform is not required
for reproducing the distributed ML analysis.

The Hough source is included for software provenance and reproducibility.

======================================================================
PART I: SOFTWARE DEPENDENCIES
======================================================================

The Python analysis scripts require a scientific Python environment with
packages including:

    numpy
    pandas
    matplotlib
    scikit-learn
    joblib

The distributed trained model was produced using the software
environment used for the original analysis. For the most reliable model
loading and numerical reproduction, use a compatible scikit-learn
environment.

The analysis scripts used during development were designed to remain
compatible with Python 3.6 where possible.


