6. RECONSTRUCT EXPERIMENTAL CENTER-OF-MASS QUANTITIES
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Run:

    python3 scripts/alpha_cm_reconstruction_static_vertices.py \
      --points-dir experimental_data/experimental_data_point_clouds \
      --vertices experimental_data/experimental_data_analysis/experimental_ml_apply/selected_vertices \
      --alpha-energy-csv experimental_data/experimental_data_analysis/alpha_energy_reconstructed/alpha_kinetic_energy.csv \
      --detector-map experimental_data/experimental_data_analysis/silicon_channel_positions_forward.csv \
      --elastic-mapping experimental_data/experimental_data_analysis/elastic_mapping.csv \
      --hough-lines-dir experimental_data/experimental_data_hough_lines \
      --output-dir experimental_data/experimental_data_analysis/alpha_cm_reconstructured \
      --exclude-radius-mm 5 \
      --beam-alpha-min 180 \
      --entrance-z-mm -80 \
      --detector-y-offset 0 \
      --detector-z-offset 0 \
      --annotate-events \
      --verbose

The reconstructed point clouds are required because the selected vertex
alone does not provide the track directions.

The script uses the point cloud to reconstruct the beam, outgoing-alpha,
and recoil directions and then determines the beam-alpha laboratory
angle and beam path.

Important outputs are:

    experimental_data/experimental_data_analysis/alpha_cm_reconstructured/
        alpha_cm_reconstruction.csv
        alpha_cm_hough_reconstruction.csv
        alpha_cm_skipped.csv
        alpha_cm_hough_skipped.csv
        alpha_cm_energy_vs_beam_path.png
        alpha_cm_hough_vs_beam_path.png
